Here's a translation of the text into uvl-Code:

```
Bicycle {
    Groupset {
        Manufacturer = [SRAM, Shimano]
    }
    Parts {
        Use-case = [Gravel, Road, Mountain]
        Gravel {
            Tyres = {Width = large, Profile = moderate}
        }
        Road {
            Tyres = {Width = narrow, Profile = none}
        }
        Mountain {
            Tyres = {Width = very_large, Profile = deep}
        }
    }
    Handlebars {
        Gravel = Drop-bar
        Road = Drop-bar
        Mountain = Flat
    }
    Optional {
        SlimTyresOnGravel = true
    }
}
``` 

This code describes a bicycle with a groupset manufactured by either SRAM or Shimano, and other parts designed for different use cases such as gravel, road, and mountain biking. The gravel bike has wider tires with some profile, while the road bike has narrower tires with no profile. Both bikes have drop bar handlebars, while the mountain bike has a flat handlebar with extra-wide tires and a deep profile. Additionally, it mentions that it is possible to fit slim tires on the gravel bike.